<article class="env-definition" id="02OJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02OJ">Definition <span data-tag="02OJ">31.2.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent sheaf on $X$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $x \in X$ is <em>associated</em> to $\mathcal{F}$ if the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_ x$ is associated to the $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$-module $\mathcal{F}_ x$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We denote $\text{Ass}(\mathcal{F})$ or $\text{Ass}_ X(\mathcal{F})$ the set of associated points of $\mathcal{F}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The <em>associated points of $X$</em> are the associated points of $\mathcal{O}_ X$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>